From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: fix the battery current sign on the TB321FU

The Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 3 (TB321FU) battery firmware reports
BATT_CURR_NOW negative while charging and positive while discharging.
UPower takes the sign over the charging status, so a charging tablet was
shown as discharging, with a time to empty in Steam instead of a time to
full. Invert it on this machine only.

Based on GUF296's fix (github.com/GUF296/linux, TB321FU-7.1.1).
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-10-13 09:20:48.744607384 +0200
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-10-13 09:21:22.685195172 +0200
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
@@ -323,6 +324,9 @@
 
 	enum qcom_battmgr_unit unit;
 
+	/* Firmware that reports the battery current negative while charging */
+	bool invert_current;
+
 	int error;
 	struct completion ack;
 
@@ -1470,6 +1474,8 @@
 			break;
 		case BATT_CURR_NOW:
 			battmgr->status.current_now = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			if (battmgr->invert_current)
+				battmgr->status.current_now = -battmgr->status.current_now;
 			break;
 		case BATT_TEMP:
 			val = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
@@ -1715,6 +1721,12 @@
 	else
 		battmgr->variant = QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350;
 
+	/*
+	 * The Lenovo TB321FU firmware reports the battery current negative
+	 * while charging: UPower then shows a charging tablet as discharging.
+	 */
+	battmgr->invert_current = of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,tb321fu");
+
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(battmgr);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
